# Key-on. 0x08 selects a channel; a write to that channel's 0x20 register
# keys all four of its operators on (bit 6 set) or off (clear). A write to
# another channel's 0x20 changes its connection but keys nothing; reselecting
# then keys. Several voices overlap, 0x20 is rewritten with the key held
# (no retrigger), and keys go off while the attack is still running.
